hadiths[56]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28111","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: My father, and it was read to Sufyan: I heard Ibn Abi Husayn, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid. Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine hunger and lying."
"28112","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: My father, and it was read to Sufyan: I heard Ibn Abi Husayn, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid. Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine hunger and lying."
"28113","Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, he heard Shahr say: I heard Asma bint Yazid, one of the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us while we were among women, and he greeted us and said: Beware and the ingratitude toward benefactors. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is ingratitude toward benefactors? He said: Perhaps one of you remains long unmarried among her parents and grows old as a spinster, then Allah Almighty provides her a husband and provides her from him wealth and children, then she becomes angry and goes saying: I never saw any good from him ever. And he said once: any good ever."
"28114","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Muhajir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not kill your children secretly, for the killing of ghayl overtakes the horseman and throws him from the back of his horse."
"28115","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Dawud al-Awdi narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah to pledge allegiance to him, and I drew near wearing two gold bracelets, and he saw their glint and said: Throw off the two bracelets, O Asma, do you not fear that Allah will encircle you with a bracelet of fire? She said: So I threw them off, and I do not know who took them."
"28116","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Dawud meaning Ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing of gold is permissible, nor its glint."
"28117","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while his armor was mortgaged."
"28118","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram al-Fazari narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, the like of it."
"28119","Waki narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Asma, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and milk was brought, and he said: Will you drink? We said: We do not desire it. He said: Do not combine lying and hunger."
"28120","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his house, and he said: When it is three years before the emergence of the Dajjal, the sky withholds a third of its rain and the earth withholds a third of its vegetation, and when it is the second year, the sky withholds two thirds of its rain and the earth withholds two thirds of its vegetation, and when it is the third year, the sky withholds all its rain and the earth withholds all its vegetation, so no hoofed or cloven-hoofed creature remains except it perishes. The Dajjal will say to a desert man: Do you see, if I resurrect your camels huge with udders, great with humps, do you know that I am your lord? He will say: Yes. Devils will appear to him in the form of his camels, and he will follow him. And he will say to a man: Do you see, if I resurrect your father and your son and whom you know of your family, do you know that I am your lord? He will say: Yes. Devils will appear to him in their forms, and he will follow him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and the people of the house wept. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned while we were weeping, and he said: What makes you weep? I said: O Messenger of Allah, what you mentioned of the Dajjal, for by Allah the slave girl of my family kneads her dough and does not reach until it almost crumbles from hunger, so how will we do on that day? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Takbir and tasbih and tahmid will suffice the believers on that day instead of food and drink. Then he said: Do not weep, for if the Dajjal emerges while I am among you, I am his disputant, and if he emerges after me, Allah is my Caliph over every Muslim."
"28121","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: Indeed he did unrighteous work, and I heard him recite: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah, indeed Allah forgives all sins and does not care, indeed He is the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"28122","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) address, saying: O people, what carries you to follow one another in lying as moths follow one another into fire? All lying is recorded against the son of Adam except three traits: a man who lies to his wife to please her, or a man who lies in a war stratagem, or a man who lies between two Muslim women to reconcile between them."
"28123","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, on the authority of Ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will remain in the earth forty years, the year like a month, and the month like a Friday, and the Friday like a day, and the day like the burning of a palm frond in fire."
"28124","Hashim, he is Ibn al-Qasim, narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: Asma bint Yazid narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the Muslim women for the pledge, and Asma said to him: Will you not uncover your hand for us, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: I do not shake hands with women, but I take upon them. And among the women was an aunt of hers wearing two gold bracelets and gold rings, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O you, would it please you that Allah adorn you on the Day of Resurrection with two bracelets and rings from the coals of Hell? She said: I seek refuge with Allah, O Prophet of Allah. She said: I said: O my aunt, throw off what is on you, and she threw it off. Asma narrated to me, by Allah, O my son, she threw it off, and I do not know who picked it up from its place, nor did anyone of us turn to it. Asma said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, one of them is disliked by her husband if she is not adorned for him or beautified for him. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is no harm upon one of you to take two earrings of silver and to take for herself two beads of silver and to roll them between her fingers with some saffron, and then it is like gold shining."
"28125","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj, that Mamar drank from knowledge most beneficial. He said: My father, and Mamar died when he was fifty-eight years old."
"28126","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, he said: Asma bint Yazid narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses, good is tied in their forelocks forever until the Day of Resurrection, so whoever ties them as preparation in the path of Allah and spends on them seeking reward in the path of Allah, then their satiety and hunger and quenching and thirst and dung and urine are success in his scales on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever ties them for showing off and repute and joy and exultation, then their satiety and hunger and quenching and thirst and dung and urine are loss in his scales on the Day of Resurrection."
"28127","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah meaning Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: I was holding the halter of al-Adba, the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the Maidah was sent down upon him entirely, and it almost broke the foreleg of the she-camel from its heaviness."
"28128","Abu al-Nadr and Hasan ibn Musa said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought drink and it was passed around the people, and among them was a fasting man, and when it reached him he said to him: Drink. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, he does not break fast and fasts perpetually. He said, meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He has not fasted who fasts forever."
"28129","Abu Amir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, and Abd al-Samad said: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Mahmud ibn Amr, that Asma bint Yazid narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who adorns herself with a necklace of gold, the like of it of fire will be placed in her neck on the Day of Resurrection, and any woman who puts in her ear an earring of gold, the like of it of fire will be placed in her ear on the Day of Resurrection. Abd al-Samad said in his hadith: He said: Mahmud ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: And any woman who puts in her ear an earring, the like of it of fire will be placed in her ear on the Day of Resurrection."
"28130","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hafs al-Sarraj narrated to us, he said: I heard Shahr ibn Hawshab narrate on the authority of Asma bint Yazid that she used to attend the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the women, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a woman wearing two gold bracelets and said to her: Would it please you that Allah encircle you with two bracelets of fire? She said: So she took them out. Asma said: By Allah, I do not know whether she removed it or I removed it."
"28131","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house and he mentioned the Dajjal and said: Before him are three years, a year in which the sky holds a third of its rain and the earth a third of its vegetation, and the second in which the sky holds two thirds of its rain and the earth two thirds of its vegetation, and the third in which the sky holds all its rain and the earth all its vegetation, so no toothed nor cloven-hoofed beast remains except it perishes. And his severest trial is that he comes to the Bedouin and says: Do you see, if I bring your camels to life for you, do you not know that I am your lord? He said: He says: Yes. Devils appear to him like his camels in the best udders and greatest humps. He said: And he comes to a man whose brother has died and whose father has died and says: Do you see, if I bring your father to life for you and bring your brother to life for you, do you not know that I am your lord? He says: Yes. Devils appear to him like his father and like his brother. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for a need, then returned. She said: And the people were in concern and grief from what he narrated to them. She said: He took the two door jambs and said: Mahyam, O Asma. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have torn our hearts with mention of the Dajjal. He said: If he emerges while I am alive, I am his disputant, otherwise my Lord is my Caliph over every believer. Asma said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah we knead our dough and do not bake it until we hunger, so how with the believers on that day? He said: What suffices the people of heaven of tasbih and taqdis will suffice them."
"28132","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Shahr narrated to us, he said: And Asma bint Yazid narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat once narrating to them about the one-eyed Dajjal, and he mentioned the like of it, and added in it, and he said: Mahyam, and it was the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he asked about something, he says: Mahyam. And he added in it: Whoever attends my gathering and hears my saying, let the witness of you convey to the absent, and know that Allah Almighty is sound, not one-eyed, and that the Dajjal is one-eyed, blind of the eye, between his eyes is written kafir, every believer reads it, literate and illiterate."
"28133","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ismail meaning Ibn Abi Khalid informed us, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Rashid, on the authority of a woman of the Ansar called Asma bint Yazid ibn Sakan, she said: When Sad ibn Muadh died, his mother cried out, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will not your tear cease and your grief go, for your son is the first for whom Allah laughed and for whom the Throne shook."
"28134","Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to me, on the authority of Thabit ibn al-Ajlan, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The aqiqah for the boy is two equal sheep, and for the girl a sheep."
"28135","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hafs al-Sarraj narrated to us, he said: I heard Shahr say: Asma bint Yazid narrated to me that she was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while men and women were sitting with him, and he said: Perhaps a man says what he does with his family, and perhaps a woman informs of what she did with her husband. The people fell silent. I said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, they say it and they do it. He said: Do not do it, for that is only like a devil meeting a she-devil on a road and he covers her while people look."
"28136","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab said: Hisham informed us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Mahmud ibn Amr, that Asma bint Yazid narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who adorns herself with a necklace of gold, the like of it of fire will be placed in her neck on the Day of Resurrection, and any woman who puts in her ear an earring of gold, the like of it will be placed in her ear on the Day of Resurrection."
"28137","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah meaning Ibn Salih narrated to us, on the authority of al-Muhajir, freedman of Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah, he said: I heard Asma bint Yazid say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not kill your children secretly, for by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it overtakes the horseman and throws him down. She said: I said: What does he mean? He said: Ghilah, a man comes to his wife while she is nursing."
"28138","Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: I heard Hammad ibn Zayd, and he mentioned the Jahmiyyah, and he said: They only attempt that there is nothing in the heaven."
"28139","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, he said: Asma bint Yazid narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died the day he died while his armor was mortgaged with a man of the Jews for a wasq of barley."
"28140","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Shahr narrated to us, he said: Asma bint Yazid narrated to me that Abu Dharr al-Ghifari used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he finished his service he sheltered in the mosque, and it was his house, he would lie in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque one night and found Abu Dharr sleeping fallen in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nudged him with his foot until he sat upright, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do I not see you sleeping? Abu Dharr said: O Messenger of Allah, where shall I sleep, have I any house other than it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat with him and said to him: How will you be when they expel you from it? He said: Then I will join Sham, for Sham is the land of migration and the land of gathering and the land of the prophets, and I will be a man of its people. He said to him: How will you be when they expel you from Sham? He said: Then I will return to it, and it will be my house and abode. He said to him: How will you be when they expel you from it the second time? He said: Then I will take my sword and fight for myself until I die. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled at him and fixed him with his hand. He said: Shall I guide you to better than that? He said: Yes, may my father and mother be for you, O Prophet of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You submit to them wherever they lead you, and you go along with them wherever they drive you, until you meet me while you are upon that."
"28141","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Shahr narrated to me, he said: I heard Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah narrate, she claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed in the mosque one day while a group of women were sitting, and he waved his hand to them with greeting. He said: Beware and ingratitude toward benefactors, beware and ingratitude toward benefactors. One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, I seek refuge with Allah, O Prophet of Allah, from ingratitude toward Allah. He said: Yes, one of you remains long unmarried and her spinsterhood lengthens, then Allah marries her to a husband and grants her children and coolness of eyes, then she becomes angry and swears by Allah she never saw an hour of good from him ever. That is of ingratitude for the blessings of Allah Almighty, and that is of ingratitude toward benefactors."
"28142","Abu al-Mughirah and Ali ibn Ayyash said: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid ibn Sakan al-Ansariyyah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not kill your children secretly, for ghayl overtakes the horseman and throws him from atop his horse. Ali said: Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned the like of it."
"28143","Abu al-Yaman informed us, Shuayb informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me that Asma bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan, one of the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, he entered upon her one day and she brought him food, and he said: I do not desire it. She said: I adorned Aishah for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I came to him and called him to her unveiling, and he came and sat beside her, and a large cup of milk was brought, and he drank, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed it to her, and she lowered her head and was shy. Asma said: So I scolded her and said to her: Take from the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: So she took and drank something. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Give your coeval. Asma said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, rather take it and drink from it, then hand it to me from your hand. He took it and drank from it, then handed it to me. She said: I sat, then I placed it on my knee, then I began to turn it and follow it with my lips to catch the drinking place of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said to women with me: Hand it to them. They said: We do not desire it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine hunger and lying. Are you ending from saying: I do not desire it? I said: O mother, I will never return ever."
"28144","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: Surah al-Maidah was sent down upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entirely, it almost from its heaviness broke the she-camel."
"28145","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever ties a horse in the path of Allah and spends on it seeking reward, its satiety and hunger and quenching and thirst and urine and dung will be in his scale on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever ties a horse for showing off and repute, that will be loss in his scale on the Day of Resurrection."
"28146","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not shake hands with women."
"28147","Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: Indeed he did unrighteous work."
"28148","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah, indeed Allah forgives all sins and does not care, indeed He is the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"28149","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Lying is not proper except in three: a man lying to his wife to please her, or lying in war, for war is deception, or lying in reconciling between people."
"28150","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Husayn, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: We were among those who prepared Aishah and escorted her. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered us milk, and we said: We do not want it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine hunger and lying."
"28151","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, on the authority of Ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of your best? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Those who when seen, Allah is remembered. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of your worst? Those who walk with slander, corrupt between loved ones, seeking hardship for the innocent."
"28152","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, on the authority of Ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will remain in the earth forty years, the year like a month, and the month like a Friday, and the Friday like a day, and the day like the burning of a palm frond in fire."
"28153","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of your best? They said: Yes. He said: Your best are those who when seen, Allah is remembered. Shall I not inform you of your worst? They said: Yes. He said: Your worst are those who corrupt between loved ones, walk with slander, seeking hardship for the innocent."
"28154","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Abd al-Jalil al-Qaysi informed us, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, that Asma bint Yazid used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: While I was with him, my aunt came to him. She said: She began to ask him, wearing two gold bracelets. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Would it please you that upon you are two bracelets of fire? She said: I said: O my aunt, he only means these two bracelets of yours. She said: So she threw them off. She said: O Prophet of Allah, they, if they do not adorn themselves, are disliked by their husbands. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: Can not one of you make a necklace of silver and a bead of silver, then perfume it with saffron, and it will be as if of gold? Whoever adorns with the weight of a locust eye of gold or drags a glint will be branded with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"28155","Dawud ibn Mihran al-Dabbagh narrated to us, Dawud meaning al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks wine, Allah will not be pleased with him forty nights, and if he dies he dies a disbeliever, and if he repents Allah turns to him, and if he returns, it is due upon Allah to give him to drink from the mud of khabal. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the mud of khabal? He said: The pus of the people of Fire."
"28156","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma, she said: I went with my aunt to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in her hand were two gold bracelets, or she said: two gold heart pendants. He said to me: Would it please you that two bracelets of fire be placed in your hand? I said to her: O my aunt, do you not hear what he says? She said: What does he say? I said: He says: Would it please you that two bracelets of fire be placed in your hands, or he said: two pendants of fire. She said: So she pulled them off and threw them, and I did not know which of the people took them."
"28157","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Mahmud ibn Amr, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who wears a necklace of gold will be necklaced with the like of it of fire on the Day of Resurrection, and any woman who puts in her ear an earring of gold, the like of it of fire will be placed in her ear on the Day of Resurrection."
"28158","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: Indeed he did unrighteous work, and she heard him recite: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah, indeed Allah forgives all sins and does not care, indeed He is the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"28159","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qaddah narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the accustomed security of Quraysh, their accustomed journey of winter and summer. Woe to you, O Quraysh, worship the Lord of this House Who fed you from hunger and secured you from fear."
"28160","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Uthman meaning Ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lying is not proper except in three: a man lying to his wife to please her, or reconciling between people, or lying in war."
"28161","Arim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever defends the flesh of his brother in backbiting, it is due upon Allah to free him from Fire."
"28162","Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever defends the flesh of his brother in backbiting, it is due upon Allah to free him from Fire."
"28163","Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about these two verses: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer, and Alif Lam Mim, Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer: Indeed in them is the Greatest Name of Allah."
"28164","Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, Aban meaning al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, on the authority of Mahmud ibn Amr, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house larger than it in Paradise."
"28165","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: Indeed Allah forgives all sins and does not care, indeed He is the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"28166","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, she said: I and my aunt entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and upon her were bracelets of gold, and he said to us: Do you give its zakat? She said: We said: No. He said: Do you not fear that Allah will encircle you with a bracelet of fire? Pay its zakat."
